.TH SOVEREIGN-AUTO 1 "May 2026" "v1.0" "Sovereign Mesh Manual"
.SH NAME
sovereign-auto \- Autonomous Mesh Orchestrator and Code-Walking Agent
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sovereign-auto
.I command
[\fIargs\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sovereign-auto
is a high-level autonomous orchestrator designed to replace traditional CLI interactions with the Sovereign Mesh. It combines the 7-layer pedigree system with the "Get Shit Done" (GSD) framework to provide autonomous code explanation, execution, and self-healing.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBwalk\fR \fIpath\fR
Recursively traverses the specified path and explains each source file (.go, .py, .proto) by retrieving its 7-layer pedigree ancestry from the Mesh Engine and GSD context from local metadata.
.TP
\fBexecute\fR \fI"goal"\fR
Initiates the GSD-Executor engine to autonomously plan, implement, and verify a high-level goal.
.TP
\fBcheck\fR \fIpath\fR
Performs an automated sanity check on the specified directory, detecting syntax errors in Go and Python files and identifying architectural deviances.
.TP
\fBfix\fR \fI"issue"\fR
Invokes the GSD-Debugger and Code-Fixer agents to autonomously diagnose and repair a specified issue or error.
.TP
\fBhelp\fR
Displays the in-CLI help manual.
.SH ARCHITECTURE
.B sovereign-auto
operates by delegating complex tasks to specialized GSD agents:
.IP \(bu 2
\fBgsd-planner:\fR For goal decomposition.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBgsd-executor:\fR For atomic implementation.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBgsd-debugger:\fR For autonomous self-healing.
.SH EXAMPLES
.B sovereign-auto walk cmd/mesh_server
.PP
.B sovereign-auto execute "Add a new endpoint to sync.proto"
.PP
.B sovereign-auto fix "Syntax error in ledger.go line 42"
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBsovereign-cli\fR(1), \fBmgsh-cli\fR(1), \fBgmudd\fR(1)
.SH AUTHOR
Sovereign Mesh Core Developers
